{"cells": [{"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Contact Book with Functions and Dictionaries\n", "\n", "## Problem\n", "\n", "You are building a **Contact Book** — a simple system to manage personal contacts. Think of it like a digital address book where you can store people's names, phone numbers, and email addresses.\n", "\n", "Your contact book should support these operations:\n", "1. **Add a contact** — store a person's name, phone number, and email\n", "2. **Search for a contact** — find and display a contact by name\n", "3. **List all contacts** — show all stored contacts in a formatted way\n", "4. **Delete a contact** — remove a contact by name\n", "5. **Update a contact** — modify an existing contact's phone or email\n", "\n", "You will use **dictionaries** to store individual contacts and a **list of dictionaries** to store all contacts. You will also use **string methods** to format output nicely and **functions** to organize your code."]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## Expected Output\n", "\n", "### Example 1: Adding and Listing Contacts\n", "\n", "When you add Alice and Bob, then list all contacts, you should see:\n", "```\n", "Contact added: Alice\n", "Contact added: Bob\n", "\n", "--- All Contacts ---\n", "1. Alice | Phone: 9876543210 | Email: alice@example.com\n", "2. Bob | Phone: 9123456789 | Email: bob@example.com\n", "```\n", "\n", "### Example 2: Searching for a Contact\n", "\n", "When you search for Charlie, you should see:\n", "```\n", "Contact found:\n", "Name: Charlie\n", "Phone: 9555555555\n", "Email: charlie@example.com\n", "```\n", "\n", "### Example 3: Updating a Contact\n", "\n", "When you update Diana's phone number, the search should show the new number:\n", "```\n", "Contact updated: Diana\n", "\n", "Contact found:\n", "Name: Diana\n", "Phone: 9222222222\n", "Email: diana@example.com\n", "```\n", "\n", "### Example 4: Deleting a Contact\n", "\n", "When you delete Eve and then search for her, you should see:\n", "```\n", "Contact deleted: Eve\n", "\n", "Contact not found.\n", "```"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## Your Task\n", "\n", "Implement the following functions in the cells below. Each function should work with a global list called `contacts` that stores all contact dictionaries.\n", "\n", "**Key Requirements:**\n", "- Contact names should be case-insensitive (\"alice\" and \"Alice\" are the same contact)\n", "- Each contact is a dictionary with keys: 'name', 'phone', 'email'\n", "- Use string methods to format output nicely\n", "- Handle cases where a contact does not exist"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Initialize the global contacts list\n", "contacts = []\n", "\n", "def add_contact(name, phone, email):\n", "    \"\"\"Add a new contact to the contact book.\"\"\"\n", "    pass\n", "\n", "def search_contact(name):\n", "    \"\"\"Search for a contact by name and display their details.\"\"\"\n", "    pass\n", "\n", "def list_all_contacts():\n", "    \"\"\"Display all contacts in the contact book.\"\"\"\n", "    pass\n", "\n", "def delete_contact(name):\n", "    \"\"\"Delete a contact from the contact book.\"\"\"\n", "    pass\n", "\n", "def update_contact(name, phone=None, email=None):\n", "    \"\"\"Update a contact's phone number and/or email.\"\"\"\n", "    pass"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## Test Your Implementation\n", "\n", "Run the cells below to test your contact book. Each cell demonstrates a different operation."]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Test 1: Add contacts\n", "print(\"=== Test 1: Adding Contacts ===")\n", "add_contact('Alice', '9876543210', 'alice@example.com')\n", "add_contact('Bob', '9123456789', 'bob@example.com')\n", "add_contact('Charlie', '9555555555', 'charlie@example.com')"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Test 2: List a